WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.301
You are

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:04.504
always in the spotlight, and yet you care

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:05.372
most about people

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.540
who are never in the spotlight.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:07.974
You care

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:08.808
most about people

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:12.379
that we as as a society have thrown away.

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:16.349
And I wonder why that is.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.754
I think experience,

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.389
maybe just life

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.524
experiences, positive or negative.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.693
Becoming a mom,

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:28.495
you know, life changes you.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.163
I you know,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.400
I think you get to a point where you

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.702
have experiences that just change you.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:38.671
And when I met Alice

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:41.975
and I felt like it was a fairly

00:00:44.511 --> 00:00:46.613
easy experience for me

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.515
when I know it shouldn't be to help

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:49.949
get someone out.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.052
It takes ten, 20 years

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:57.590
to do what I did in six months.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:01.061
And I didn't realize

00:01:02.295 --> 00:01:04.431
the fight at that time.

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.067
To me, that was a few phone calls,

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.936
and that really struck me

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:14.007
that, you know, however it was done,

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:15.175
it was done.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.043
I'm so grateful.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.612
But like that that the system,

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.748
that process has to change.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.849
I think you're selling

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:23.950
yourself short, though,

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.152
because Van Jones,

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:29.122
one of your biggest cheerleaders,

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.792
good friend of ours at CNN,

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.427
told me this about you.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.329
There is nobody like Kim.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.465
She is in a category of her own.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:39.566
She takes every case

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.500
so seriously,

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.534
she'll have read the file

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.736
with more care than the attorneys.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.405
She will know the case backwards

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:48.408
and forwards in every meeting.

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:50.610
Do you think this will be your life's

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.879
most meaningful work ahead?

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.614
I hope so.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:55.615
I hope so.

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.118
I always joke with my mom,

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.152
who's my manager.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:01.821
I say Kim K is retiring

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.289
and I'm just going to be an attorney.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:05.358
Kim, Esquire. Yes.

00:02:06.559 --> 00:02:07.060
So I was like,

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.230
so you can go help my siblings.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:11.297
Are you.

00:02:12.332 --> 00:02:13.800
So you can still have like,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:17.003
what about my 10% or

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:18.304
so? I'm giving her the heads up.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.506
Are you

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.141
would you ever consider a life

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:23.076
without the cameras?

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.310
Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:27.881
I do feel like I have a

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.215
there's a lot

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.284
that's always on TV and a lot

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:32.252
that's always out there.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.620
But I think my friends

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:35.622
and my family know we really cherish

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.692
a lot of our private times and

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.928
I would be just as happy

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:43.863
being an attorney full time

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:46.633
and doing that.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.969
The journey just really opened up my eyes

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:52.172
to so much that I just

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.140
it gets overwhelming

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:56.709
because there's so much to be done.

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.111
And I just,

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:58.378
you know,

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:59.979
I brought my sister Chloe to a prison

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.548
for the first time last week,

00:03:01.548 --> 00:03:04.117
and that was really eye opening for her.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:06.920
And I just

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:07.620
I would

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.622
totally spend more time doing that.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.425
Cameras. No cameras.

